---
import "../styles.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — Clash-free class picker</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <p class="site-title">Clash-free class picker</p>
      <p class="site-disclaimer">Student project · not an official ANU system</p>
    </header>
    <nav aria-label="site">
      <a href="/">Plan</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
    </nav>
    <main>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>
        This is a clash-aware class picker. It rebuilds one slice of ANU
        class registration (ISIS / MyTimetable): choosing which lecture,
        tutorial or crit group you go to for each course.
      </p>
      <p>
        Enrolment week is the worst week. Everyone logs in at once. The site
        slows down, keeps loading, or freezes. I still can't see all my
        class times in one place — I check lectures and tutorials against
        each other by hand, and it's easy to miss a clash. Usually I find it
        after I've picked, when the good groups are already full.
      </p>
      <p>Demo timetable — times are invented. Built for COMP4020 C7.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
